    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `initials` field following the existing `displayName` pattern in this codebase.\n\n**Where the logic went** \u2014 `Person.java` (the `@MappedSuperclass` shared by `Owner`), right next to the analogous `getDisplayName()`:\n\n```java\npublic String getInitials() {\n    return initial(this.firstName) + \".\" + initial(this.lastName) + \".\";\n}\n\nprivate static String initial(String name) {\n    return name.substring(0, 1).toUpperCase();\n}\n```\n\nThis keeps the derivation as a single-responsibility computed getter on the domain model, so it's inherited by `Owner` (and any other `Person` subtype) rather than duplicated.\n\n**Exposure** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml`, mirroring `displayName`. The generated `OwnerDto` picks it up, and MapStruct's `OwnerMapper.toOwnerDto` maps `owner.getInitials()` \u2192 `dto.initials` automatically (same mechanism `displayName` already relies on) \u2014 no controller or mapper changes needed.\n\n**Verification** \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials` (creating `john`/`smith`, asserting `$.initials == \"J.S.\"`) and the full `./mvnw test` run both pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
